<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Batutulis inscription</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1533</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Batutulis inscription is an Old Sundanese stone inscription in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogor">Bogor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a>, set up in 1533 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surawisesa">Surawisesa</a> in memory of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-baduga-maharaja">Sri Baduga Maharaja</a>. It praises the late king for building a moat around the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakuan-pajajaran">Pakuan Pajajaran</a>, raising an artificial hill, creating a sacred forest and making a lake, and is a key source for the history of the Sunda Kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/batutulis-inscription.jpg" alt="Batutulis inscription" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RXerself, Creutzen · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batutulis_Inscription_inside.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
